%!PS-Adobe-3.0
%%Title: drycrayon.ps — wax crayon on paper, and a child's ways of drawing with it
%%Creator: pscat — issue #239 (design: docs/DRYMEDIA.md)
%%EndComments
% @requires: (lib/artkit.ps) run (lib/paintkit.ps) run (lib/drykit.ps) run

% The crayon medium of epic #232, built on drykit's core (lib/drykit.ps):
% every mark is `dkstroke` on a `dksurface`, and this file only decides how
% a wax crayon presses, what paper it is drawn on, and how a child moves it.
% It never edits lib/drykit.ps.
%
% Public:
%
%   opts  dypaper     crayon paper: drykit's /construction tooth, coarser,
%                     on a white ground (the reference crops' paper)
%   /name dycolor     sets the current colour from the crayon box (dybox)
%   opts  dycrayon    draws the current path in wax crayon, current colour
%
% and the child-drawing motions, the dry-media counterpart of paintkit's
% #184 generators. Each builds a path and paints nothing, so it composes
% with dycrayon (or any preset that inks a path):
%
%   opts         dywobble    a shaky, overshooting version of the current path
%   region opts  dyscribble  back-and-forth scribble fill over a region
%   cx cy r opts dyloop      a circle drawn in one loop that doesn't close
%   x y h opts   dyfigure    a stick (or tadpole) figure
%   cx cy r opts dyrays      quick sun rays around a disc
%   opts         dygrass     quick grass blades along the current path
%
% The motions keep paintkit's contract (lib/paintkit.ps, "Brush motions"):
% each *replaces* the current path; none paints or touches colour; all draw
% only from artkit's `frnd`, so they are deterministic under the caller's
% own `srand` and `--sweep-seed` varies the composition while the texture
% (drykit's, seeded from the canvas) stays put. Every slot (a subpath, a
% pass, a loop, a limb, a ray, a blade) takes a fixed number of `frnd`
% draws, and any randomness whose amount depends on a slot's length (a
% tremor sampled along a line) comes from a private generator seeded by one
% of those draws. So a knob that reshapes one slot never re-rolls where the
% later ones land. Each is bounded by a work budget, rejected by a
% self-documenting guard.
%
% How the crayon presses (dycrayon), from the reference board
% (docs/drymedia/REFERENCES.md, Y1-Y6):
%
% * Waxy coverage (Y1, Y2). The tip deposits only where it meets raised
%   tooth, and a skipped valley streaks along the travel (drykit's oriented
%   catch, /Streak about 2). A crayon tip is rounded, so it presses hardest
%   at its centre: each stroke is a dense core plus a wider rim at lower
%   touch, which gives the ragged, speckled edge of a real crayon line
%   instead of a clean capsule.
% * Pressure along a stroke (Y4). A child presses on landing and fades
%   toward the lift, with an uneven, wandering pressure in between.
% * Wax build-up (Y3). A turn or a reversal slows the hand and presses
%   harder: /Buildup raises the touch where the walked path turns.
% * Repeated passes. Drykit can't read the page back, so a later pass over
%   the same area is declared with /Pass: each pass presses wax into more
%   of the tooth. Passes must be drawn inside one `dkbatch`, or the second
%   pass's faint level greys the first one's core (DRYMEDIA.md 3.3).
% * Layering. Wax slides on wax, so a colour laid over another (/Over)
%   catches less and the colour beneath shows through its gaps.
% * Tip wear (Y6). /Worn is how blunt the crayon is: a new point has a
%   narrow dense core in a wide ragged rim; a worn flat face is wider and
%   presses evenly across. /Wear widens the contact along each stroke,
%   drykit's meaning.
% * One deposit level. Wax is opaque and leaves no dust, so a crayon has
%   none of chalk's tone ramp (drykit's M4): each of the core and the rim
%   is a single drykit level. That is also half the catches.
%
% dycrayon draws each subpath as its own pair of dkstroke calls (the touch
% profile depends on the subpath's own turns), all inside one dkbatch, so
% the call stays level-major. If the caller already has a dkbatch open,
% dycrayon adds to it instead of opening one (batches don't nest). It tells
% the two apart by `userdict /dkBatch`, drykit's open-batch record; the
% `drycrayon-drykit-contract` self-test pins that.
%
% Determinism. dycrayon takes no draws from the caller's `rand`: its own
% randomness (the phase of the uneven pressure) comes from a private
% Schrage generator, seeded per subpath from /Seed or from the subpath's
% first point on the canvas, as drykit seeds a stroke.
%
% Scratch prefixes: dy- (shared helpers), dyK (dycrayon), dyT (its touch
% profile), dyC (path collection), dyW (wobble lines), dyS (dyscribble),
% dyL (dyloop), dyF (dyfigure), dyR (dyrays), dyG (dygrass). None is a
% prefix drykit or paintkit uses.

% --- helpers ----------------------------------------------------------

% any -> bool   (an integer or a real)
% @internal
/dyisnum {
    type dup /integertype eq exch /realtype eq or
} def

% any -> bool   (an executable array or packed array: a procedure)
% @internal
/dyisproc {
    dup xcheck exch type dup /arraytype eq exch /packedarraytype eq or and
} def

% dict key default -> value   (the default when the key is absent)
% @internal
/dyget {
    /dygd exch def
    2 copy known { get } { pop pop /dygd load } ifelse
} def

% dict key default lo hi /error -> number   (a number option in lo..hi)
% Anything else, a procedure included, raises the error by name.
% @internal
/dyoptnum {
    /dyoe exch def /dyoh exch def /dyol exch def
    dyget
    dup dyisnum not { pop dyoe cvx exec } if
    dup dyol lt 1 index dyoh gt or { pop dyoe cvx exec } if
} def

% dict key default lo hi /error -> integer   (a whole number in lo..hi)
% @internal
/dyoptint {
    dup /dyoie exch def
    dyoptnum
    dup dup cvi ne { pop dyoie cvx exec } if
    cvi
} def

% dict key default /error -> bool
% @internal
/dyoptbool {
    /dyoe exch def
    dyget
    dup type /booleantype ne { pop dyoe cvx exec } if
} def

% value /error -> [r g b]   (an rgb array of three numbers 0..1, copied)
% @internal
/dyrgb {
    /dyoe exch def
    dup type /arraytype ne 1 index type /packedarraytype ne and { dyoe cvx exec } if
    dup xcheck { dyoe cvx exec } if
    dup length 3 ne { dyoe cvx exec } if
    dup {
        dup dyisnum not { pop dyoe cvx exec } if
        dup 0 lt exch 1 gt or { dyoe cvx exec } if
    } forall
    aload pop 3 array astore
} def

% a b -> max(a, b)
% @internal
/dymax {
    2 copy lt { exch } if pop
} def

% a b -> min(a, b)
% @internal
/dymin {
    2 copy gt { exch } if pop
} def

% x lo hi -> x clamped to lo..hi
% @internal
/dyclamp {
    /dych exch def /dycl exch def
    dup dycl lt { pop dycl } if
    dup dych gt { pop dych } if
} def

% any -> bool   (an artkit region: screct or scpath)
% @internal
/dyisregion {
    dup type /dicttype eq
        { dup /BBox known exch /Kind known and }
        { pop false }
    ifelse
} def

% seed -   (seeds drycrayon's own generator)
% The same Schrage-form minimal standard LCG as paintkit's pjrand and
% drykit's dkrand, under its own state, so both interpreters draw the same
% sequence and the caller's `rand` stream is never touched.
% @internal
/dysrand {
    cvi 2147483646 mod abs 1 add
    userdict /dystate 3 -1 roll put
} def

% -> 0.0..1.0   (exclusive at both ends)
% @internal
/dyrand {
    userdict /dystate get
    dup 127773 idiv 2836 mul exch 127773 mod 16807 mul exch sub
    dup 0 lt { 2147483647 add } if
    dup userdict /dystate 3 -1 roll put
    2147483647 div
} def

userdict /dystate 2 put

% -> integer 0..999999   (one caller draw, as a seed for dysrand)
% @internal
/dyslotseed {
    frnd 999999 mul cvi
} def

% --- the crayon box ---------------------------------------------------

% The colours of a standard 16-crayon box, in box order, as sRGB. They are
% a wax crayon's colours on white paper rather than paint primaries: a
% little muted, the yellow warm, the white faintly grey.
% @kind: Constant
% @summary: The crayon box: a dict of 16 named crayon colours (rgb arrays), the colours of a standard 16-crayon box as they read on white paper. Iterate them in box order with dycolors; set one with dycolor.
% @example: dybox /bluegreen get aload pop setrgbcolor
/dybox <<
    /red          [0.84 0.16 0.20]
    /redorange    [0.95 0.36 0.20]
    /orange       [0.98 0.53 0.16]
    /yelloworange [1.00 0.70 0.26]
    /yellow       [0.99 0.87 0.22]
    /yellowgreen  [0.66 0.81 0.30]
    /green        [0.18 0.61 0.33]
    /bluegreen    [0.08 0.57 0.62]
    /blue         [0.16 0.41 0.79]
    /blueviolet   [0.38 0.34 0.70]
    /violet       [0.53 0.31 0.66]
    /redviolet    [0.73 0.23 0.50]
    /carnation    [0.98 0.62 0.72]
    /brown        [0.61 0.36 0.21]
    /black        [0.14 0.13 0.13]
    /white        [0.96 0.96 0.94]
>> def

% @kind: Constant
% @summary: The names of the crayon box's 16 colours, in box order (dybox has no order of its own): red, red-orange, orange, yellow-orange, yellow, yellow-green, green, blue-green, blue, blue-violet, violet, red-violet, carnation pink, brown, black, white.
% @example: dycolors { dycolor ... } forall
/dycolors [
    /red /redorange /orange /yelloworange /yellow /yellowgreen /green
    /bluegreen /blue /blueviolet /violet /redviolet /carnation /brown
    /black /white
] def

%%SelfTest: dycolor-guards
%   { (red) dycolor } /dycolor-needs-a-colour-name
%   (a string for the name) mustguard
%
%   { /mauve dycolor } /dycolor-unknown-colour
%   (a name not in the box) mustguard
%
%   { /blue dycolor } (a colour in the box) mustpass
%   currentrgbcolor 0.79 sub abs 0.001 lt exch 0.41 sub abs 0.001 lt and
%   exch 0.16 sub abs 0.001 lt and
%   (dycolor sets the box's rgb) mustbe
%
%   dycolors length 16 eq (the box holds sixteen) mustbe
%   true dycolors { dybox exch known and } forall
%   (every name in dycolors is in dybox) mustbe
%   dybox length 16 eq (and dybox holds nothing else) mustbe
%%EndSelfTest
%
% @kind: Procedure
% @summary: Sets the current colour to a crayon from the box (dybox): /red, /redorange, /orange, /yelloworange, /yellow, /yellowgreen, /green, /bluegreen, /blue, /blueviolet, /violet, /redviolet, /carnation, /brown, /black or /white. dycrayon then draws in it.
% @example: /green dycolor newpath 40 40 moveto 200 60 lineto << >> dycrayon
/dycolor {
    dup type /nametype ne { pop dycolor-needs-a-colour-name } if
    dybox 1 index known not { pop dycolor-unknown-colour } if
    dybox exch get aload pop setrgbcolor
} def

% --- paper ------------------------------------------------------------

%%SelfTest: dypaper-sets-crayon-paper
%   { 5 dypaper } /dypaper-options-must-be-a-dict
%   (a number for the options) mustguard
%
%   << >> dypaper
%   userdict /dkSurface get /construction eq userdict /pjW get 1.4 eq and
%   userdict /pjR get 0.65 eq and userdict /pjM get 8 eq and
%   (the defaults: construction paper's tooth, coarser) mustbe
%   userdict /dkGround get 0 get 0.97 eq (on a white ground) mustbe
%
%   << /Weave 1 /Ground [0.2 0.3 0.8] >> dypaper
%   userdict /pjW get 1 eq userdict /pjR get 0.65 eq and
%   userdict /dkGround get 2 get 0.8 eq and
%   (a key given replaces its default and keeps the rest) mustbe
%
%   { << /Surface /marble >> dypaper } /dksurface-unknown-surface
%   (dksurface's own guards still apply) mustguard
%%EndSelfTest
%
% @kind: Procedure
% @summary: Sets up crayon paper as the drykit surface: drykit's construction-paper tooth made coarser and softer, on a white ground, tuned against the crayon reference crops (docs/drymedia/REFERENCES.md Y1, Y2) so a light scribble leaves a quarter to a third of the paper showing in streaks and a heavy one is nearly solid. Takes dksurface's keys, any of which replaces the default; paints nothing (paint the ground yourself) and takes no rand draws.
% @example: << /Seed 4 >> dypaper 0.97 0.96 0.93 setrgbcolor clippath fill
% @param: /Surface [name] The drykit surface underneath, as dksurface (default /construction)
% @param: /Seed [integer] Seed for the paper's tooth, as dksurface (default 1)
% @param: /Weave [points] Tooth spacing, as dksurface (default 1.4: a child's cheap paper, coarser than drykit's 0.9)
% @param: /Mottle [points] Scale of the slow variation in the tooth, as dksurface (default 8)
% @param: /Relief [0..1] How much the slow mottle decides which tooth stands proud, as dksurface (default 0.65)
% @param: /Ground [rgb array] The paper's colour, which crayon strokes read as what lies beneath, as dksurface (default a warm white [0.97 0.96 0.93])
/dypaper {
    dup type /dicttype ne { pop dypaper-options-must-be-a-dict } if
    /dypo exch def
    <<
        /Surface /construction
        /Ground [0.97 0.96 0.93]
        /Weave 1.4
        /Relief 0.65
        /Mottle 8
    >>
    dup dypo { 3 copy put pop pop } forall
    pop dksurface
} def

% --- dycrayon ---------------------------------------------------------

% How far below the core's touch a crayon's rim presses, for a new point
% (Worn 0) and a worn flat (Worn 1); and how wide the dense core is, as a
% fraction of /Width, at the same two ends.
% @internal
/dyKrim0 0.16 def
% @internal
/dyKrim1 0.06 def
% @internal
/dyKcore0 0.5 def
% @internal
/dyKcore1 0.85 def

% Touch added to every crayon level. dkstroke's faint level sits 0.12
% above its touch (DRYMEDIA.md 3.3), so a crayon's single level, raised by
% the same, covers the tooth a two-level dkstroke at the same /Touch
% covers: /Touch keeps drykit's meaning.
% @internal
/dyKlift 0.12 def

% Touch added per pass after the first, and taken away when wax slides on
% an earlier colour (/Over).
% @internal
/dyKpassstep 0.06 def
% @internal
/dyKresist 0.08 def

% Subpaths one dycrayon call may draw (each is two dkstroke calls).
% @internal
/dyKmaxsubs 20000 def

% t base isproc land fade uneven build L W p1 p2 turns pitch offset -> touch
% The crayon's touch at t (0..1 along the subpath): the base (a number, or
% the caller's {t -> touch}), a landing press over the first 2 Widths, a
% fade toward the lift, a slow wander in two incommensurate waves, the
% build-up at the walked turn nearest t, and a fixed offset (passes,
% wax on wax, the rim). Clamped to 0..1.
% @internal
/dyTat {
    /dyToff exch def /dyTpitch exch def /dyTturn exch def
    /dyTp2 exch def /dyTp1 exch def /dyTW exch def /dyTL exch def
    /dyTbuild exch def /dyTuneven exch def /dyTfade exch def /dyTland exch def
    /dyTisp exch def /dyTbase exch def /dyTt exch def
    dyTisp {
        dyTt /dyTbase load exec
        dup dyisnum not { pop dycrayon-touch-procedure-must-return-a-number } if
    } { dyTbase } ifelse
    /dyTs dyTt dyTL mul def
    1 dyTs dyTW 2 mul div sub dup 0 lt { pop 0 } if dyTland mul add
    dyTfade dyTt mul sub
    dyTp1 dyTs 8 mul add sin 0.6 mul dyTp2 dyTs 21.2 mul add sin 0.4 mul add
    dyTuneven mul add
    dyTturn length 0 gt {
        dyTs dyTpitch div round cvi 0 dyTturn length 1 sub dyclamp
        dyTturn exch get dyTbuild mul add
    } if
    dyToff add
    0 1 dyclamp
} def

% -> [ [x y x y ...] ... ]   (the current path, flattened, as point lists)
% A closepath repeats the subpath's first point, so a closed outline is
% walked all the way round, as dkstroke would walk it.
% @internal
/dyKsubpaths {
    flattenpath
    mark
    /dyKopen false def
    {
        /dyKsy exch def /dyKsx exch def
        dyKopen { counttomark array astore exch pop } if
        mark dyKsx dyKsy
        /dyKopen true def
    }
    { }
    { pop pop pop pop pop pop }
    { dyKsx dyKsy }
    pathforall
    dyKopen { counttomark array astore exch pop } if
    counttomark array astore exch pop
    newpath
} def

% P -   (the point list as a fresh path)
% @internal
/dyKpath {
    /dyKpp exch def
    newpath
    dyKpp 0 get dyKpp 1 get moveto
    1 1 dyKpp length 2 idiv 1 sub {
        2 mul dup dyKpp exch get exch 1 add dyKpp exch get lineto
    } for
} def

% -   (one subpath, dyKP, as a core and a rim: dyKk is its index)
% @internal
/dyKone {
    dyKP dyKpath
    % Its own walk, at the rim's pitch: length and the turn at each stop.
    /dyKpitch dyKw 0.75 mul 1 4 dyclamp def
    /dyKn 0 def
    dyKpitch { pop pop pop pop pop pop /dyKn dyKn 1 add def } walkpath
    /dyKang dyKn array def
    /dyKi 0 def /dyKL 0 def
    dyKpitch {
        pop /dyKsp exch def pop dyKang dyKi 3 -1 roll put pop pop
        dyKi 0 gt { /dyKL dyKL dyKsp add def } if
        /dyKi dyKi 1 add def
    } walkpath
    % Turning per stop (0 at a straight stop, 1 at a reversal), summed over
    % three stops so a curved turn counts as much as a sharp one, then
    % spread one stop either side: the hand slows before and after.
    /dyKd dyKn array def
    0 1 dyKn 1 sub {
        /dyKi exch def
        dyKi 0 eq {
            0
        } {
            % walkpath's headings are atan's 0..360, so the gap is at most 360
            dyKang dyKi get dyKang dyKi 1 sub get sub abs
            dup 180 gt { 360 exch sub } if
        } ifelse
        dyKd dyKi 3 -1 roll put
    } for
    /dyKturn [
        0 1 dyKn 1 sub {
            /dyKi exch def
            0
            dyKi 1 sub 1 dyKi 1 add {
                dup 0 ge 1 index dyKn lt and { dyKd exch get add } { pop } ifelse
            } for
            120 div 1 dymin
        } for
    ] def
    /dyKturn [
        0 1 dyKn 1 sub {
            /dyKi exch def
            dyKturn dyKi get
            dyKi 0 gt { dyKturn dyKi 1 sub get 0.7 mul dymax } if
            dyKi dyKn 1 sub lt { dyKturn dyKi 1 add get 0.7 mul dymax } if
        } for
    ] def
    % seed: /Seed + k, or the first point's canvas position (drykit's rule)
    dyKhasseed {
        /dyKs dyKseed cvi dyKk add def
    } {
        dyKP 0 get dyKP 1 get transform userdict /pjCTM get itransform
        100 mul round dup abs 2e9 gt { pop 0 } if cvi 46337 mod abs
        exch
        100 mul round dup abs 2e9 gt { pop 0 } if cvi 46337 mod abs
        exch 46337 mul add
        /dyKs exch def
    } ifelse
    dyKs 7907 add dysrand
    /dyKp1 dyrand 360 mul def
    /dyKp2 dyrand 360 mul def
    /dyKbonus dyKpass 1 sub dyKpassstep mul dyKhasover { dyKresist sub } if dyKlift add def
    /dyKrimoff dyKrim0 dyKrim1 dyKrim0 sub dyKworn mul add neg def
    % a new point draws 0.8 Width, a worn flat 1.2 Width
    /dyKww dyKw 0.8 0.4 dyKworn mul add mul def
    % Rim, then core: both in the open batch, so level-major together.
    dyKP dyKpath
    << /Width dyKww /Touch dyKrimoff false dyKtouch
       /Bands 16 /Levels 1 /Halo 0 /Streak dyKstreak /Strength dyKstrength
       /Wear dyKwear /Under dyKunder
       dyKhasseed { /Seed dyKs } if >> dkstroke
    dyKP dyKpath
    << /Width dyKww dyKcore0 dyKcore1 dyKcore0 sub dyKworn mul add mul
       /Touch 0 true dyKtouch
       /Bands 16 /Levels 1 /Halo 0
       /Streak dyKstreak /Strength dyKstrength
       /Wear dyKwear /Under dyKunder
       dyKhasseed { /Seed dyKs 1000003 add } if >> dkstroke
} def

% offset core -> touch-or-procedure   (the subpath's touch for dkstroke)
% A plain number when nothing varies along the stroke, so dkstroke draws
% one band; otherwise a procedure closing over this subpath's profile.
% The landing and the build-up press the core only: pushing harder drives
% the middle of the tip into the valleys while its rounded edge still
% skims the tooth, so a pressed spot is dense inside a ragged edge rather
% than a solid disc.
% @internal
/dyKtouch {
    /dyKcore exch def /dyKoff exch def
    /dyKl dyKcore { dyKland } { 0 } ifelse def
    /dyKb dyKcore { dyKbuild } { 0 } ifelse def
    dyKtp not dyKl 0 eq and dyKfade 0 eq and dyKuneven 0 eq and dyKb 0 eq and {
        dyKt dyKbonus add dyKoff add 0 1 dyclamp
    } {
        [ /dyKt load dyKtp dyKl dyKfade dyKuneven dyKb
          dyKL dyKw dyKp1 dyKp2 dyKturn dyKpitch dyKbonus dyKoff add
          /dyTat cvx ] cvx
    } ifelse
} def

% -   (every subpath of dyKsubs)
% @internal
/dyKdraw {
    0 1 dyKsubs length 1 sub {
        /dyKk exch def
        /dyKP dyKsubs dyKk get def
        dyKone
    } for
} def

%%SelfTest: dycrayon-rejects-malformed-options
%   << >> dypaper
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto 5 dycrayon } /dycrayon-options-must-be-a-dict
%   (a number for the options) mustguard
%
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /Width 0 >> dycrayon } /dycrayon-width-must-be-positive
%   (/Width 0) mustguard
%
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /Touch 1.2 >> dycrayon } /dycrayon-touch-must-be-0-to-1
%   (/Touch 1.2) mustguard
%
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /Touch (hard) >> dycrayon } /dycrayon-touch-must-be-a-number-or-procedure
%   (a string /Touch) mustguard
%
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /Touch { pop (x) } >> dycrayon }
%   /dycrayon-touch-procedure-must-return-a-number
%   (a /Touch procedure returning a string) mustguard
%
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /Landing { 0.2 } >> dycrayon } /dycrayon-landing-must-be-0-to-1
%   (a procedure /Landing) mustguard
%
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /Fade -0.1 >> dycrayon } /dycrayon-fade-must-be-0-to-1
%   (/Fade -0.1) mustguard
%
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /Uneven 2 >> dycrayon } /dycrayon-uneven-must-be-0-to-1
%   (/Uneven 2) mustguard
%
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /Buildup 1.5 >> dycrayon } /dycrayon-buildup-must-be-0-to-1
%   (/Buildup 1.5) mustguard
%
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /Worn 3 >> dycrayon } /dycrayon-worn-must-be-0-to-1
%   (/Worn 3) mustguard
%
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /Wear 5 >> dycrayon } /dycrayon-wear-must-be-0-to-4
%   (/Wear 5) mustguard
%
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /Pass 1.5 >> dycrayon } /dycrayon-pass-must-be-1-to-8
%   (a fractional /Pass) mustguard
%
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /Pass 9 >> dycrayon } /dycrayon-pass-must-be-1-to-8
%   (/Pass 9) mustguard
%
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /Streak 0.5 >> dycrayon } /dycrayon-streak-must-be-1-to-4
%   (/Streak 0.5) mustguard
%
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /Strength 2 >> dycrayon } /dycrayon-strength-must-be-0-to-1
%   (/Strength 2) mustguard
%
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /Over [1 0] >> dycrayon } /dycrayon-over-must-be-an-rgb-array
%   (a two-entry /Over) mustguard
%
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /Seed (s) >> dycrayon } /dycrayon-seed-must-be-a-number
%   (a string /Seed) mustguard
%
%   % A procedure /Touch is a procedure whether or not it was packed.
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /Touch [ /pop cvx 0.7 ] cvx >> dycrayon }
%   (a procedure /Touch) mustpass
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto
%     true setpacking << /Touch { pop 0.7 } >> false setpacking dycrayon }
%   (a packed procedure /Touch) mustpass
%
%   { newpath << >> dycrayon } (an empty path draws nothing) mustpass
%%EndSelfTest
%
%%SelfTest: dycrayon-needs-a-surface
%   userdict /dkGround undef
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << >> dycrayon } /dycrayon-needs-a-surface
%   (no dksurface or dypaper yet) mustguard
%%EndSelfTest
%
%%SelfTest: dycrayon-takes-no-draws-and-joins-an-open-batch
%   << >> dypaper
%   7 srand rand /dyta exch def
%   7 srand newpath 0 0 moveto 30 10 lineto 0 20 lineto 40 40 moveto 60 40 lineto
%   << /Seed 3 >> dycrayon rand dyta eq
%   (dycrayon leaves the caller's stream untouched) mustbe
%
%   7 srand newpath 0 0 moveto 30 10 lineto 0 20 lineto << >> dycrayon rand dyta eq
%   (with the position seed too) mustbe
%
%   { { newpath 0 0 moveto 30 10 lineto << >> dycrayon
%       newpath 0 5 moveto 30 15 lineto << /Pass 2 >> dycrayon } dkbatch }
%   (two dycrayon calls inside one open dkbatch) mustpass
%
%   { { newpath 0 0 moveto 30 10 lineto << >> dycrayon
%       1 0 0 setrgbcolor newpath 0 5 moveto 30 15 lineto << >> dycrayon } dkbatch }
%   /dkbatch-mixes-pigments
%   (a second colour in the caller's batch is drykit's error) mustguard
%   userdict /dkBatch known not (and the batch is closed after it) mustbe
%%EndSelfTest
%
%%SelfTest: drycrayon-drykit-contract
%   % dycrayon joins a batch the caller opened by reading drykit's open-batch
%   % record. If drykit renames it, dycrayon would nest a batch and raise
%   % dkbatch-cannot-nest inside every caller's batch: this fails first.
%   /dyctin false def
%   { /dyctin userdict /dkBatch known def } dkbatch
%   dyctin (an open dkbatch is userdict /dkBatch) mustbe
%   userdict /dkBatch known not (and it is gone when the batch ends) mustbe
%   << >> dypaper
%   userdict /dkGround known userdict /pjCTM known and
%   (a surface leaves /dkGround and paintkit's /pjCTM in userdict) mustbe
%%EndSelfTest
%
% @kind: Procedure
% @summary: Draws the current path in wax crayon, in the current colour, on the drykit surface (dypaper is crayon paper): the wax catches only on the paper's tooth, leaving white specks that streak along the stroke, and a rounded tip gives a dense core with a ragged rim. A child's pressure profile (a press on landing, a fade, an uneven wander) and wax build-up where the stroke turns or reverses are on by default. Repeated passes (/Pass) build coverage and a colour laid over another (/Over) lets it show through; draw passes or several calls of one colour inside one dkbatch. Consumes the current path like fill; takes no rand draws from the caller's stream.
% @example: << >> dypaper /blue dycolor newpath 40 40 moveto 120 80 lineto 200 50 lineto << /Width 6 /Touch 0.7 >> dycrayon
% @param: /Width [points] Contact width of a half-worn crayon (/Worn 0.5); must be > 0 (default 6)
% @param: /Touch [0..1] Pressure against the tooth, drykit's meaning: low catches only the highest tooth, 1 is solid. A procedure {t -> touch}, t = 0..1 along each subpath, is a base profile that the landing, fade, wander and build-up are added to (default 0.75)
% @param: /Landing [0..1] Extra touch at the middle of the tip where each stroke lands, fading over its first two Widths (default 0.08)
% @param: /Fade [0..1] How much the touch falls from the start of each stroke to its end, as the hand lifts (default 0.12)
% @param: /Uneven [0..1] How far the touch wanders along each stroke, a child's uneven pressure (default 0.06)
% @param: /Buildup [0..1] Extra touch at the middle of the tip where the stroke turns or reverses, as the hand slows and wax builds up; a full reversal gets all of it (default 0.15)
% @param: /Worn [0..1] How blunt the crayon is: 0 is a new point, a line 0.8 /Width wide with a narrow dense core in a ragged rim; 1 is a worn flat face, 1.2 /Width wide, pressing evenly across (default 0.4)
% @param: /Wear [fraction of /Width] How much wider the contact gets from the start of each subpath to its end as the tip wears, drykit's meaning, 0..4 (default 0.1)
% @param: /Pass [count] Which pass over the same area this is, 1..8: each later pass presses wax into more of the tooth. Draw the passes inside one dkbatch (default 1)
% @param: /Over [rgb array] The crayon colour this stroke is laid over. Wax slides on wax, so the stroke catches less and the colour beneath shows through its gaps. It is drykit's /Under for the stroke: where the stroke runs past the colour onto bare paper it is tinted toward it by 1 - /Strength (default unset: laid on the paper)
% @param: /Streak [ratio] How much each tooth knuckle is stretched along the stroke, drykit's meaning, 1..4: skipped valleys read as streaks (default 2.2)
% @param: /Strength [0..1] How strongly the wax reads against the paper, drykit's meaning (default 0.95)
% @param: /Seed [integer] Seed for the stroke's own randomness (the wander, drykit's tool side); subpath i uses Seed + i. Leaves the caller's rand stream untouched (default from each subpath's first point on the canvas)
/dycrayon {
    dup type /dicttype ne { pop dycrayon-options-must-be-a-dict } if
    /dyKo exch def
    userdict /dkGround known not { dycrayon-needs-a-surface } if
    /dyKw dyKo /Width 6 1e-6 1e6 /dycrayon-width-must-be-positive dyoptnum def
    /dyKt dyKo /Touch 0.75 dyget def
    /dyKt load dyisproc {
        /dyKtp true def
    } {
        /dyKtp false def
        /dyKt load dyisnum not { dycrayon-touch-must-be-a-number-or-procedure } if
        dyKt 0 lt dyKt 1 gt or { dycrayon-touch-must-be-0-to-1 } if
    } ifelse
    /dyKland dyKo /Landing 0.08 0 1 /dycrayon-landing-must-be-0-to-1 dyoptnum def
    /dyKfade dyKo /Fade 0.12 0 1 /dycrayon-fade-must-be-0-to-1 dyoptnum def
    /dyKuneven dyKo /Uneven 0.06 0 1 /dycrayon-uneven-must-be-0-to-1 dyoptnum def
    /dyKbuild dyKo /Buildup 0.15 0 1 /dycrayon-buildup-must-be-0-to-1 dyoptnum def
    /dyKworn dyKo /Worn 0.4 0 1 /dycrayon-worn-must-be-0-to-1 dyoptnum def
    /dyKwear dyKo /Wear 0.1 0 4 /dycrayon-wear-must-be-0-to-4 dyoptnum def
    /dyKpass dyKo /Pass 1 1 8 /dycrayon-pass-must-be-1-to-8 dyoptint def
    /dyKstreak dyKo /Streak 2.2 1 4 /dycrayon-streak-must-be-1-to-4 dyoptnum def
    /dyKstrength dyKo /Strength 0.95 0 1 /dycrayon-strength-must-be-0-to-1 dyoptnum def
    dyKo /Over known {
        /dyKhasover true def
        /dyKunder dyKo /Over get /dycrayon-over-must-be-an-rgb-array dyrgb def
    } {
        /dyKhasover false def
        /dyKunder userdict /dkGround get def
    } ifelse
    dyKo /Seed known {
        /dyKhasseed true def
        /dyKseed dyKo /Seed get def
        /dyKseed load dyisnum not { dycrayon-seed-must-be-a-number } if
        dyKseed abs 2147483647 ge { dycrayon-seed-must-be-within-integer-range } if
    } { /dyKhasseed false def } ifelse

    /dyKsubs dyKsubpaths def
    dyKsubs length dyKmaxsubs gt { dycrayon-too-many-subpaths } if
    dyKsubs length 0 gt {
        userdict /dkBatch known
            { dyKdraw }
            { { dyKdraw } dkbatch }
        ifelse
    } if
} def

% --- motions: shared pieces --------------------------------------------

% pitch cap {guard} dyCcollect -
% Walks the current path (flattened) and stores every stop as
% [x y ang t sp atend] in dyCs, its length in dyCn. Counts first, with the
% budget check inside the callback, then fills a preallocated array.
% @internal
/dyCcollect {
    /dyCg exch def /dyCcap exch def /dyCp exch def
    /dyCn 0 def
    dyCp {
        pop pop pop pop pop pop
        /dyCn dyCn 1 add def
        dyCn dyCcap gt { dyCg } if
    } walkpath
    /dyCs dyCn array def
    /dyCi 0 def
    dyCp {
        6 array astore dyCs dyCi 3 -1 roll put
        /dyCi dyCi 1 add def
    } walkpath
} def

% -> [ [a b] ... ]   (index ranges of dyCs, one per subpath)
% @internal
/dyCsubs {
    /dyCst [
        0 1 dyCn 1 sub {
            dup dyCs exch get 5 get dup 1 eq exch 3 eq or { } { pop } ifelse
        } for
    ] def
    [
        0 1 dyCst length 1 sub {
            /dyCk exch def
            dyCst dyCk get
            dyCk 1 add dyCst length lt { dyCst dyCk 1 add get 1 sub } { dyCn 1 sub } ifelse
            2 array astore
        } for
    ]
} def

% P amp lambda tremor overshoot -   (appends one wobbly line)
% P is a flat [x y x y ...] list sampled finely along the line. Takes six
% frnd draws (two wave phases, two overshoot lengths, the hook, a seed for
% the tremor), whatever the line's length. The line wanders sideways in
% two incommensurate waves of about `lambda`, shakes by up to `tremor` at
% every sample, starts a little before its first point and runs past its
% last by up to `overshoot`, hooking as the hand swings off.
% @internal
/dyWline {
    /dyWover exch def /dyWtrem exch def /dyWlam exch def /dyWamp exch def
    /dyWP exch def
    /dyWp1 frnd 360 mul def
    /dyWp2 frnd 360 mul def
    /dyWfe frnd def
    /dyWfs frnd def
    /dyWfh frnd def
    dyslotseed dysrand
    /dyWp3 dyrand 360 mul def
    /dyWn dyWP length 2 idiv def
    dyWn 0 gt {
        % the offset line
        /dyWQ dyWn 2 mul array def
        /dyWs 0 def
        0 1 dyWn 1 sub {
            /dyWi exch def
            /dyWx dyWP dyWi 2 mul get def
            /dyWy dyWP dyWi 2 mul 1 add get def
            dyWi 0 gt {
                /dyWs dyWs
                    dyWx dyWP dyWi 1 sub 2 mul get sub dup mul
                    dyWy dyWP dyWi 1 sub 2 mul 1 add get sub dup mul add sqrt
                add def
            } if
            % tangent from the neighbours (one-sided at the ends)
            /dyWa dyWi 1 sub 0 dymax def
            /dyWb dyWi 1 add dyWn 1 sub dymin def
            /dyWtx dyWP dyWb 2 mul get dyWP dyWa 2 mul get sub def
            /dyWty dyWP dyWb 2 mul 1 add get dyWP dyWa 2 mul 1 add get sub def
            /dyWtl dyWtx dup mul dyWty dup mul add sqrt def
            dyWtl 0 gt {
                /dyWtx dyWtx dyWtl div def /dyWty dyWty dyWtl div def
            } { /dyWtx 1 def /dyWty 0 def } ifelse
            % Two waves at lambda and 0.43 lambda, their sum swelling and
            % shrinking under a third, slower one, so the wander never
            % settles into a regular ripple.
            /dyWo
                dyWp1 dyWs dyWlam div 360 mul add sin 0.65 mul
                dyWp2 dyWs dyWlam 0.43 mul div 360 mul add sin 0.35 mul add
                dyWp3 dyWs dyWlam 2.7 mul div 360 mul add sin 0.45 mul 0.75 add mul
                dyWamp mul
                dyrand 2 mul 1 sub dyWtrem mul add
            def
            dyWQ dyWi 2 mul dyWx dyWty dyWo mul sub put
            dyWQ dyWi 2 mul 1 add dyWy dyWtx dyWo mul add put
        } for
        % heading at either end of the offset line
        dyWn 1 gt {
            /dyWh1 dyWQ dyWn 2 mul 1 sub get dyWQ dyWn 2 mul 3 sub get sub
                   dyWQ dyWn 2 mul 2 sub get dyWQ dyWn 2 mul 4 sub get sub
                   2 copy 0 eq exch 0 eq and { pop pop 0 } { atan } ifelse def
            /dyWh0 dyWQ 1 get dyWQ 3 get sub dyWQ 0 get dyWQ 2 get sub
                   2 copy 0 eq exch 0 eq and { pop pop 180 } { atan } ifelse def
        } { /dyWh1 0 def /dyWh0 180 def } ifelse
        % a short lead-in before the first point
        /dyWe0 dyWover 0.3 mul dyWfs mul def
        dyWQ 0 get dyWh0 cos dyWe0 mul add
        dyWQ 1 get dyWh0 sin dyWe0 mul add moveto
        0 1 dyWn 1 sub { 2 mul dup dyWQ exch get exch 1 add dyWQ exch get lineto } for
        dyWn 1 eq dyWover 0 eq and { dyWQ 0 get dyWQ 1 get lineto } if
        % the overshoot: three steps, turning by the hook
        /dyWe1 dyWover 0.4 dyWfe 0.8 mul add mul def
        dyWe1 0 gt {
            /dyWhk dyWfh 2 mul 1 sub 30 mul def
            /dyWcx dyWQ dyWn 2 mul 2 sub get def
            /dyWcy dyWQ dyWn 2 mul 1 sub get def
            1 1 3 {
                /dyWh1 dyWh1 dyWhk 3 div add def
                /dyWcx dyWcx dyWh1 cos dyWe1 3 div mul add def
                /dyWcy dyWcy dyWh1 sin dyWe1 3 div mul add def
                dyWcx dyWcy lineto
                pop
            } for
        } if
    } if
} def

% x0 y0 x1 y1 amp lambda tremor overshoot -   (dyWline along a segment)
% @internal
/dyWseg {
    /dyWsv exch def /dyWst exch def /dyWsl exch def /dyWsa exch def
    /dyWy1 exch def /dyWx1 exch def /dyWy0 exch def /dyWx0 exch def
    /dyWlen dyWx1 dyWx0 sub dup mul dyWy1 dyWy0 sub dup mul add sqrt def
    /dyWk dyWlen 2 div ceiling cvi 1 dymax 2000 dymin def
    [ 0 1 dyWk {
        dyWk div /dyWf exch def
        dyWx0 dyWx1 dyWx0 sub dyWf mul add
        dyWy0 dyWy1 dyWy0 sub dyWf mul add
    } for ]
    dyWsa dyWsl dyWst dyWsv dyWline
} def

% --- dywobble ------------------------------------------------------------

%%SelfTest: dywobble-guards
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto 5 dywobble } /dywobble-options-must-be-a-dict
%   (a number for the options) mustguard
%
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /Wobble -1 >> dywobble } /dywobble-wobble-must-be-non-negative
%   (/Wobble -1) mustguard
%
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /Wobble { 2 } >> dywobble } /dywobble-wobble-must-be-non-negative
%   (a procedure /Wobble) mustguard
%
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /Wavelength 0 >> dywobble } /dywobble-wavelength-must-be-positive
%   (/Wavelength 0) mustguard
%
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /Tremor -1 >> dywobble } /dywobble-tremor-must-be-non-negative
%   (/Tremor -1) mustguard
%
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /Overshoot -1 >> dywobble } /dywobble-overshoot-must-be-non-negative
%   (/Overshoot -1) mustguard
%
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 1000000 0 lineto << /Wavelength 0.1 >> dywobble }
%   /dywobble-point-count-exceeds-safety-limit
%   (a tiny wavelength on a long line) mustguard
%
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto 0 10 moveto 0 60 lineto << >> dywobble
%     newpath 5 5 moveto << >> dywobble newpath << >> dywobble }
%   (two subpaths, a lone point and an empty path) mustpass
%
%   % Deterministic under the caller's srand, and it replaces the path.
%   3 srand newpath 0 0 moveto 80 0 lineto << >> dywobble pathbbox 4 array astore /dyta exch def
%   3 srand newpath 0 0 moveto 80 0 lineto << >> dywobble pathbbox 4 array astore /dytb exch def
%   true 0 1 3 { dup dyta exch get exch dytb exch get eq and } for
%   (the same srand gives the same wobble) mustbe
%   newpath 0 0 moveto 80 0 lineto << /Overshoot 0 /Tremor 0 >> dywobble
%   pathbbox pop pop pop 0 ge (no lead-in without an overshoot) mustbe
%%EndSelfTest
%
% @kind: Procedure
% @summary: A child's wobbly line: the current path is read as a spine and replaced with a shaky version of each subpath -- a slow sideways wander, a fine tremor, a short lead-in, and an overshoot past the end that hooks as the hand swings off. A closed outline runs past its start. Builds a path and paints nothing, so it composes with dycrayon: `opts dywobble << >> dycrayon`. Deterministic under the caller's own srand, with six draws per subpath.
% @example: newpath 40 60 moveto 240 70 lineto << /Wobble 2 /Overshoot 8 >> dywobble << >> dycrayon
% @param: /Wobble [points] How far the line wanders to either side of the spine; must be >= 0 (default 1.5)
% @param: /Wavelength [points] Distance along the line of one slow wander; must be > 0 (default 40)
% @param: /Tremor [points] The fine shake at every sample, to either side; must be >= 0 (default 0.3)
% @param: /Overshoot [points] How far each line runs past its end (about 0.4 to 1.2 times this), with a short lead-in before its start; must be >= 0 (default 5)
/dywobble {
    dup type /dicttype ne { pop dywobble-options-must-be-a-dict } if
    /dyWO exch def
    /dyWOa dyWO /Wobble 1.5 0 1e6 /dywobble-wobble-must-be-non-negative dyoptnum def
    /dyWOl dyWO /Wavelength 40 1e-6 1e6 /dywobble-wavelength-must-be-positive dyoptnum def
    /dyWOt dyWO /Tremor 0.3 0 1e6 /dywobble-tremor-must-be-non-negative dyoptnum def
    /dyWOv dyWO /Overshoot 5 0 1e6 /dywobble-overshoot-must-be-non-negative dyoptnum def
    % Samples every twelfth of a wander, at most 2 apart.
    dyWOl 12 div 2 dymin 200000 { dywobble-point-count-exceeds-safety-limit } dyCcollect
    newpath
    dyCsubs {
        aload pop /dyWOb exch def /dyWOf exch def
        [ dyWOf 1 dyWOb { dyCs exch get dup 0 get exch 1 get } for ]
        dyWOa dyWOl dyWOt dyWOv dyWline
    } forall
} def

% --- dyscribble ------------------------------------------------------------

%%SelfTest: dyscribble-guards
%   { 7 << >> dyscribble } /dyscribble-needs-a-region
%   (a number for the region) mustguard
%
%   { 0 0 100 50 screct 5 dyscribble } /dyscribble-options-must-be-a-dict
%   (a number for the options) mustguard
%
%   { 0 0 100 50 screct << /Spacing 0 >> dyscribble } /dyscribble-spacing-must-be-positive
%   (/Spacing 0) mustguard
%
%   { 0 0 100 50 screct << /Overrun -1 >> dyscribble } /dyscribble-overrun-must-be-non-negative
%   (/Overrun -1) mustguard
%
%   { 0 0 100 50 screct << /Miss 2 >> dyscribble } /dyscribble-miss-must-be-0-to-1
%   (/Miss 2) mustguard
%
%   { 0 0 100 50 screct << /Scatter -1 >> dyscribble } /dyscribble-scatter-must-be-non-negative
%   (/Scatter -1) mustguard
%
%   { 0 0 100 50 screct << /Direction (up) >> dyscribble } /dyscribble-direction-must-be-a-number
%   (a string /Direction) mustguard
%
%   { 0 0 100000 100000 screct << /Spacing 1 >> dyscribble }
%   /dyscribble-too-many-passes
%   (a tiny spacing over a huge region) mustguard
%
%   { 0 0 100 50 screct << /Direction 30 >> dyscribble
%     newpath 0 0 moveto 60 0 lineto 30 40 lineto closepath scpath << >> dyscribble }
%   (a rectangle at an angle and a triangle) mustpass
%
%   newpath 10 10 moveto 20 20 lineto 0 0 100 50 screct << /Miss 0 /Overrun 0 /Scatter 0 >> dyscribble
%   pathbbox 4 2 roll pop pop 50 le exch 100 le and
%   (without overrun or scatter the scribble stays in its box; the old path is gone) mustbe
%%EndSelfTest
%
% @kind: Procedure
% @summary: A child's scribble fill over a region (artkit's screct or scpath): one continuous back-and-forth line of passes /Spacing apart, each running past the region's edge by up to /Overrun before it turns, with some turns falling short (/Miss) and the passes uneven, so the fill goes outside the lines and leaves gaps. Each pass spans the region's outer extent along it, so a concave notch is scribbled over. Replaces the current path; paints nothing, so `region opts dyscribble << >> dycrayon`. Deterministic under the caller's own srand, with four draws per pass.
% @example: 60 60 160 90 screct << /Spacing 5 /Overrun 4 >> dyscribble << /Width 7 /Touch 0.65 >> dycrayon
% @param: /Spacing [points] Distance between passes, across them; must be > 0 (default 4)
% @param: /Direction [degrees] Heading of the passes, counterclockwise from +x in user space (default 0: side to side)
% @param: /Overrun [points] How far a turn runs past the region's edge, 0.3 to 1 times this; must be >= 0 (default 3)
% @param: /Miss [0..1] Chance that a turn falls short of the edge, leaving a gap there (default 0.15)
% @param: /Scatter [points] Random offset of each turn across the passes, so the passes are not parallel; must be >= 0 (default 1)
/dyscribble {
    1 index dyisregion not { dyscribble-needs-a-region } if
    dup type /dicttype ne { pop pop dyscribble-options-must-be-a-dict } if
    /dySO exch def /dySR exch def
    /dySsp dySO /Spacing 4 1e-6 1e6 /dyscribble-spacing-must-be-positive dyoptnum def
    /dySdir dySO /Direction 0 -1e6 1e6 /dyscribble-direction-must-be-a-number dyoptnum def
    /dySover dySO /Overrun 3 0 1e6 /dyscribble-overrun-must-be-non-negative dyoptnum def
    /dySmiss dySO /Miss 0.15 0 1 /dyscribble-miss-must-be-0-to-1 dyoptnum def
    /dySscat dySO /Scatter 1 0 1e6 /dyscribble-scatter-must-be-non-negative dyoptnum def
    /dySc dySdir cos def /dySs dySdir sin def
    % the region's box in the passes' frame: u along, v across
    dySR /BBox get aload pop
    /dySy1 exch def /dySx1 exch def /dySy0 exch def /dySx0 exch def
    /dySu0 1e30 def /dySu1 -1e30 def /dySv0 1e30 def /dySv1 -1e30 def
    [ dySx0 dySy0 dySx1 dySy0 dySx1 dySy1 dySx0 dySy1 ] aload pop
    4 {
        /dySy exch def /dySx exch def
        dySx dySc mul dySy dySs mul add
        dup dySu0 lt { dup /dySu0 exch def } if
        dup dySu1 gt { dup /dySu1 exch def } if pop
        dySy dySc mul dySx dySs mul sub
        dup dySv0 lt { dup /dySv0 exch def } if
        dup dySv1 gt { dup /dySv1 exch def } if pop
    } repeat
    /dySrows dySv1 dySv0 sub dySsp div floor cvi 1 add def
    dySrows 5000 gt { dyscribble-too-many-passes } if
    % 160 samples along each pass find where it enters and leaves
    /dySk 160 def
    /dySdu dySu1 dySu0 sub dySk div def
    newpath
    /dySopen false def
    /dySside 1 def
    0 1 dySrows 1 sub {
        /dySr exch def
        /dySfo frnd def /dySfm frnd def /dySfd frnd def /dySfs frnd def
        /dySv dySv0 dySv1 add 2 div dySr dySrows 1 sub 2 div sub dySsp mul add def
        /dySa 1e30 def /dySb -1e30 def
        0 1 dySk {
            dySdu mul dySu0 add /dySu exch def
            dySu dySc mul dySv dySs mul sub
            dySu dySs mul dySv dySc mul add
            dySR scin {
                dySu dySa lt { /dySa dySu def } if
                dySu dySb gt { /dySb dySu def } if
            } if
        } for
        dySa dySb le {
            /dySspan dySb dySa sub def
            /dySvv dySv dySfs 2 mul 1 sub dySscat mul add def
            dySopen not {
                % the first pass starts on the far side of where it turns
                dySside 0 gt { dySa dySover 0.5 mul sub } { dySb dySover 0.5 mul add } ifelse
                /dySu exch def
                dySu dySc mul dySvv dySs mul sub
                dySu dySs mul dySvv dySc mul add moveto
                /dySopen true def
            } if
            dySfm dySmiss lt {
                dySside 0 gt
                    { dySb dySspan 0.1 dySfd 0.3 mul add mul sub }
                    { dySa dySspan 0.1 dySfd 0.3 mul add mul add } ifelse
            } {
                dySside 0 gt
                    { dySb dySover 0.3 dySfo 0.7 mul add mul add }
                    { dySa dySover 0.3 dySfo 0.7 mul add mul sub } ifelse
            } ifelse
            /dySu exch def
            dySu dySc mul dySvv dySs mul sub
            dySu dySs mul dySvv dySc mul add lineto
            /dySside dySside neg def
        } {
            % a pass that misses the region ends this run of the line
            /dySopen false def
        } ifelse
    } for
} def

% --- dyloop ------------------------------------------------------------

% cx cy r gap squash lean wobble clockwise -   (appends one loop)
% Six frnd draws: where it starts, how far short or past, the drift in
% radius, the lean, two wobble phases.
% @internal
/dyLloop {
    /dyLcw exch def /dyLwob exch def /dyLlean exch def /dyLsq exch def
    /dyLgap exch def /dyLr exch def /dyLcy exch def /dyLcx exch def
    /dyLa0 90 frnd 2 mul 1 sub 40 mul add def
    /dyLsweep 360 frnd 2 mul 1 sub dyLgap mul add def
    /dyLdrift frnd 2 mul 1 sub 0.08 mul def
    /dyLtilt frnd 2 mul 1 sub dyLlean mul def
    /dyLq1 frnd 360 mul def
    /dyLq2 frnd 360 mul def
    /dyLn dyLsweep 6 div ceiling cvi 1 dymax def
    0 1 dyLn {
        /dyLk exch def
        /dyLf dyLk dyLn div def
        /dyLa dyLa0 dyLsweep dyLf mul dyLcw { sub } { add } ifelse def
        /dyLrr dyLr 1 dyLdrift dyLf mul add mul
            dyLq1 dyLa 2 mul add sin 0.6 mul dyLq2 dyLa 3 mul add sin 0.4 mul add
            dyLwob mul add def
        /dyLx dyLa cos dyLrr mul def
        /dyLy dyLa sin dyLrr mul dyLsq mul def
        dyLcx dyLx dyLtilt cos mul add dyLy dyLtilt sin mul sub
        dyLcy dyLx dyLtilt sin mul add dyLy dyLtilt cos mul add
        dyLk 0 eq { moveto } { lineto } ifelse
    } for
} def

%%SelfTest: dyloop-guards
%   { 50 50 (r) << >> dyloop } /dyloop-needs-three-numbers
%   (a string radius) mustguard
%
%   { 50 50 0 << >> dyloop } /dyloop-radius-must-be-positive
%   (a zero radius) mustguard
%
%   { 50 50 10 5 dyloop } /dyloop-options-must-be-a-dict
%   (a number for the options) mustguard
%
%   { 50 50 10 << /Gap 200 >> dyloop } /dyloop-gap-must-be-0-to-180
%   (/Gap 200) mustguard
%
%   { 50 50 10 << /Squash 0 >> dyloop } /dyloop-squash-must-be-0-exclusive-to-1
%   (/Squash 0) mustguard
%
%   { 50 50 10 << /Lean -1 >> dyloop } /dyloop-lean-must-be-non-negative
%   (/Lean -1) mustguard
%
%   { 50 50 10 << /Wobble -1 >> dyloop } /dyloop-wobble-must-be-non-negative
%   (/Wobble -1) mustguard
%
%   { 50 50 10 << /Clockwise 1 >> dyloop } /dyloop-clockwise-must-be-a-boolean
%   (a number /Clockwise) mustguard
%
%   newpath 0 0 moveto 1 1 lineto 50 50 10 << /Gap 0 /Lean 0 /Wobble 0 >> dyloop
%   pathbbox 4 2 roll 39 ge exch 39 ge and 3 1 roll 61 le exch 61 le and and
%   (a loop at its radius; the old path is gone) mustbe
%%EndSelfTest
%
% @kind: Procedure
% @summary: A circle as a child draws it: one loop, started near the top, that doesn't close -- it stops short of its start or runs past it (up to /Gap degrees either way), drifts a little in radius so the ends miss, leans, squashes and wobbles. Replaces the current path; paints nothing, so `cx cy r opts dyloop << >> dycrayon`. Deterministic under the caller's own srand, with six draws.
% @example: 150 150 40 << /Gap 30 >> dyloop << /Width 5 >> dycrayon
% @param: /Gap [degrees] How far the end may fall short of the start or run past it, 0..180 (default 25)
% @param: /Squash [ratio] Height of the loop as a fraction of its width, > 0 and <= 1 (default 0.9)
% @param: /Lean [degrees] Random lean of the loop's long axis; must be >= 0 (default 20)
% @param: /Wobble [points] How far the outline wavers from a smooth ellipse; must be >= 0 (default 4% of the radius)
% @param: /Clockwise [boolean] Draw the loop clockwise (default false)
/dyloop {
    dup type /dicttype ne { pop dyloop-options-must-be-a-dict } if
    3 index dyisnum 3 index dyisnum and 2 index dyisnum and
        not { pop dyloop-needs-three-numbers } if
    /dyLO exch def /dyLOr exch def /dyLOy exch def /dyLOx exch def
    dyLOr 0 le { dyloop-radius-must-be-positive } if
    /dyLOg dyLO /Gap 25 0 180 /dyloop-gap-must-be-0-to-180 dyoptnum def
    /dyLOs dyLO /Squash 0.9 0 1 /dyloop-squash-must-be-0-exclusive-to-1 dyoptnum def
    dyLOs 0 le { dyloop-squash-must-be-0-exclusive-to-1 } if
    /dyLOl dyLO /Lean 20 0 1e6 /dyloop-lean-must-be-non-negative dyoptnum def
    /dyLOw dyLO /Wobble dyLOr 0.04 mul 0 1e6 /dyloop-wobble-must-be-non-negative dyoptnum def
    /dyLOc dyLO /Clockwise false /dyloop-clockwise-must-be-a-boolean dyoptbool def
    newpath
    dyLOx dyLOy dyLOr dyLOg dyLOs dyLOl dyLOw dyLOc dyLloop
} def

% --- dyfigure ------------------------------------------------------------

%%SelfTest: dyfigure-guards
%   { 50 (y) 80 << >> dyfigure } /dyfigure-needs-three-numbers
%   (a string y) mustguard
%
%   { 50 0 -5 << >> dyfigure } /dyfigure-height-must-be-positive
%   (a negative height) mustguard
%
%   { 50 0 80 [ ] dyfigure } /dyfigure-options-must-be-a-dict
%   (an array for the options) mustguard
%
%   { 50 0 80 << /Tadpole 1 >> dyfigure } /dyfigure-tadpole-must-be-a-boolean
%   (a number /Tadpole) mustguard
%
%   { 50 0 80 << /Arms 120 >> dyfigure } /dyfigure-arms-must-be-minus-80-to-80
%   (/Arms 120) mustguard
%
%   { 50 0 80 << /Hair 2.5 >> dyfigure } /dyfigure-hair-must-be-0-to-40
%   (a fractional /Hair) mustguard
%
%   { 50 0 80 << /Wobble -1 >> dyfigure } /dyfigure-wobble-must-be-non-negative
%   (/Wobble -1) mustguard
%
%   { 50 0 80 << /Overshoot -1 >> dyfigure } /dyfigure-overshoot-must-be-non-negative
%   (/Overshoot -1) mustguard
%
%   { 50 0 80 << /Tadpole true /Hair 9 >> dyfigure 50 0 80 << >> dyfigure }
%   (a tadpole with hair, and a stick figure) mustpass
%
%   % The figure stands on y and is about h tall.
%   50 0 80 << /Wobble 0 /Overshoot 0 >> dyfigure pathbbox
%   72 ge exch pop exch -3 ge and exch pop
%   (a stick figure from its feet to the top of its head) mustbe
%%EndSelfTest
%
% @kind: Procedure
% @summary: A child's figure, standing on (x, y), about h tall: a head drawn as one loop that doesn't close, and wobbly overshooting limbs. A stick figure has a body line with arms and legs on it; a tadpole figure (/Tadpole true), the way a three-year-old draws one, grows arms and legs straight out of a big head. Optional hair is a row of short strokes over the head. Replaces the current path; paints nothing, so `x y h opts dyfigure << >> dycrayon`. Deterministic under the caller's own srand, with a fixed number of draws per part.
% @example: 120 40 140 << /Tadpole true /Hair 8 >> dyfigure << /Width 3 >> dycrayon
% @param: /Tadpole [boolean] Arms and legs grow from a big head, with no body (default false)
% @param: /Arms [degrees] Angle of the arms above the horizontal, -80..80; negative droops (default 15)
% @param: /Hair [count] Short strokes of hair over the head, whole number 0..40 (default 0)
% @param: /Wobble [points] How far each limb wanders from straight; must be >= 0 (default 1.5% of h)
% @param: /Overshoot [points] How far each limb runs past its end; must be >= 0 (default 4% of h)
/dyfigure {
    dup type /dicttype ne { pop dyfigure-options-must-be-a-dict } if
    3 index dyisnum 3 index dyisnum and 2 index dyisnum and
        not { pop dyfigure-needs-three-numbers } if
    /dyFO exch def /dyFh exch def /dyFy exch def /dyFx exch def
    dyFh 0 le { dyfigure-height-must-be-positive } if
    /dyFtad dyFO /Tadpole false /dyfigure-tadpole-must-be-a-boolean dyoptbool def
    /dyFarms dyFO /Arms 15 -80 80 /dyfigure-arms-must-be-minus-80-to-80 dyoptnum def
    /dyFhair dyFO /Hair 0 0 40 /dyfigure-hair-must-be-0-to-40 dyoptint def
    /dyFwob dyFO /Wobble dyFh 0.015 mul 0 1e6 /dyfigure-wobble-must-be-non-negative dyoptnum def
    /dyFov dyFO /Overshoot dyFh 0.04 mul 0 1e6 /dyfigure-overshoot-must-be-non-negative dyoptnum def
    /dyFlam dyFh 0.5 mul def
    newpath
    dyFtad {
        /dyFhr dyFh 0.3 mul def
        /dyFcy dyFy dyFh add dyFhr sub def
        dyFx dyFcy dyFhr 25 0.92 15 dyFhr 0.04 mul false dyLloop
        % legs from the bottom of the head
        [ -1 1 ] {
            /dyFsd exch def
            dyFx dyFsd dyFh 0.09 mul mul add dyFcy dyFhr 0.97 mul sub
            dyFx dyFsd dyFh 0.13 mul mul add dyFy
            dyFwob dyFlam dyFwob 0.2 mul dyFov dyWseg
        } forall
        % arms from the sides of the head
        [ -1 1 ] {
            /dyFsd exch def
            /dyFay dyFcy dyFhr 0.15 mul sub def
            dyFx dyFsd dyFhr 0.95 mul mul add dyFay
            dyFx dyFsd dyFhr dyFh 0.38 mul add mul add
            dyFay dyFh 0.38 mul dyFarms sin mul dyFarms cos div add
            dyFwob dyFlam dyFwob 0.2 mul dyFov dyWseg
        } forall
    } {
        /dyFhr dyFh 0.13 mul def
        /dyFcy dyFy dyFh add dyFhr sub def
        dyFx dyFcy dyFhr 25 0.92 15 dyFhr 0.04 mul false dyLloop
        /dyFneck dyFcy dyFhr 0.95 mul sub def
        /dyFhip dyFy dyFh 0.42 mul add def
        dyFx dyFneck dyFx dyFhip dyFwob dyFlam dyFwob 0.2 mul dyFov 0.5 mul dyWseg
        [ -1 1 ] {
            /dyFsd exch def
            dyFx dyFhip dyFx dyFsd dyFh 0.16 mul mul add dyFy
            dyFwob dyFlam dyFwob 0.2 mul dyFov dyWseg
        } forall
        /dyFsh dyFneck dyFh 0.08 mul sub def
        [ -1 1 ] {
            /dyFsd exch def
            dyFx dyFsh
            dyFx dyFsd dyFh 0.3 mul mul add
            dyFsh dyFh 0.3 mul dyFarms sin mul dyFarms cos div add
            dyFwob dyFlam dyFwob 0.2 mul dyFov dyWseg
        } forall
    } ifelse
    % hair: short strokes over the top of the head, from the outline out
    1 1 dyFhair {
        /dyFi exch def
        /dyFa 90 55 sub 110 dyFi 0.5 sub dyFhair div mul add def
        /dyFl dyFh 0.07 mul dyFhr 0.25 mul add def
        dyFx dyFa cos dyFhr 0.95 mul mul add dyFcy dyFa sin dyFhr 0.95 mul mul add
        dyFx dyFa cos dyFhr dyFl add mul add dyFcy dyFa sin dyFhr dyFl add mul add
        dyFwob 0.5 mul dyFlam dyFwob 0.1 mul dyFov 0.3 mul dyWseg
    } for
} def

% --- dyrays ------------------------------------------------------------

%%SelfTest: dyrays-guards
%   { 50 50 (r) << >> dyrays } /dyrays-needs-three-numbers
%   (a string radius) mustguard
%
%   { 50 50 0 << >> dyrays } /dyrays-radius-must-be-positive
%   (a zero radius) mustguard
%
%   { 50 50 10 5 dyrays } /dyrays-options-must-be-a-dict
%   (a number for the options) mustguard
%
%   { 50 50 10 << /Count 0 >> dyrays } /dyrays-count-must-be-1-to-2000
%   (/Count 0) mustguard
%
%   { 50 50 10 << /Count 2.5 >> dyrays } /dyrays-count-must-be-1-to-2000
%   (a fractional /Count) mustguard
%
%   { 50 50 10 << /Length 0 >> dyrays } /dyrays-length-must-be-positive
%   (/Length 0) mustguard
%
%   { 50 50 10 << /LengthJitter 2 >> dyrays } /dyrays-lengthjitter-must-be-0-to-1
%   (/LengthJitter 2) mustguard
%
%   { 50 50 10 << /Offset -1 >> dyrays } /dyrays-offset-must-be-non-negative
%   (/Offset -1) mustguard
%
%   { 50 50 10 << /Lean -1 >> dyrays } /dyrays-lean-must-be-non-negative
%   (/Lean -1) mustguard
%
%   { 50 50 10 << /Wander 3 >> dyrays } /dyrays-wander-must-be-0-to-1
%   (/Wander 3) mustguard
%
%   newpath 50 50 10 << /Count 8 >> dyrays
%   /dyct 0 def { pop pop /dyct dyct 1 add def } { pop pop } { 6 { pop } repeat } { } pathforall
%   dyct 8 eq
%   (eight rays are eight strokes) mustbe
%%EndSelfTest
%
% @kind: Procedure
% @summary: A child's sun rays: /Count quick straight strokes around a disc of radius r at (cx, cy), starting a little off its edge, unevenly spaced, leaning and of uneven length. Replaces the current path; paints nothing, so `cx cy r opts dyrays << >> dycrayon` (draw the disc with dyloop or dyscribble). Deterministic under the caller's own srand, with four draws per ray.
% @example: 300 300 40 << /Count 14 /Length 30 >> dyrays << /Width 5 >> dycrayon
% @param: /Count [count] How many rays, whole number 1..2000 (default 12)
% @param: /Length [points] Mean ray length; must be > 0 (default the radius)
% @param: /LengthJitter [fraction of /Length] 0..1 how far each ray's length varies around /Length (default 0.35)
% @param: /Offset [points] Mean gap between the disc's edge and where a ray starts, 0.5 to 1.5 times this; must be >= 0 (default a fifth of the radius)
% @param: /Lean [degrees] Random lean of each ray away from pointing straight out; must be >= 0 (default 8)
% @param: /Wander [fraction of the ray spacing] 0..1 how far each ray slides around the disc from its even slot (default 0.25)
/dyrays {
    dup type /dicttype ne { pop dyrays-options-must-be-a-dict } if
    3 index dyisnum 3 index dyisnum and 2 index dyisnum and
        not { pop dyrays-needs-three-numbers } if
    /dyRO exch def /dyRr exch def /dyRy exch def /dyRx exch def
    dyRr 0 le { dyrays-radius-must-be-positive } if
    /dyRn dyRO /Count 12 1 2000 /dyrays-count-must-be-1-to-2000 dyoptint def
    /dyRl dyRO /Length dyRr 1e-6 1e6 /dyrays-length-must-be-positive dyoptnum def
    /dyRj dyRO /LengthJitter 0.35 0 1 /dyrays-lengthjitter-must-be-0-to-1 dyoptnum def
    /dyRg dyRO /Offset dyRr 0.2 mul 0 1e6 /dyrays-offset-must-be-non-negative dyoptnum def
    /dyRlean dyRO /Lean 8 0 1e6 /dyrays-lean-must-be-non-negative dyoptnum def
    /dyRw dyRO /Wander 0.25 0 1 /dyrays-wander-must-be-0-to-1 dyoptnum def
    newpath
    0 1 dyRn 1 sub {
        /dyRi exch def
        /dyRfw frnd def /dyRfl frnd def /dyRfj frnd def /dyRfg frnd def
        /dyRa dyRi 360 mul dyRn div 90 add dyRfw 2 mul 1 sub dyRw mul 360 mul dyRn div add def
        /dyRd dyRr dyRg 0.5 dyRfg add mul add def
        /dyRh dyRa dyRfl 2 mul 1 sub dyRlean mul add def
        /dyRlen dyRl 1 dyRfj 2 mul 1 sub dyRj mul add mul def
        /dyRsx dyRx dyRa cos dyRd mul add def
        /dyRsy dyRy dyRa sin dyRd mul add def
        dyRsx dyRsy moveto
        dyRsx dyRh cos dyRlen mul add dyRsy dyRh sin dyRlen mul add lineto
    } for
} def

% --- dygrass ------------------------------------------------------------

%%SelfTest: dygrass-guards
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto 5 dygrass } /dygrass-options-must-be-a-dict
%   (a number for the options) mustguard
%
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /Spacing 0 >> dygrass } /dygrass-spacing-must-be-positive
%   (/Spacing 0) mustguard
%
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /Length 0 >> dygrass } /dygrass-length-must-be-positive
%   (/Length 0) mustguard
%
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /LengthJitter -1 >> dygrass } /dygrass-lengthjitter-must-be-0-to-1
%   (/LengthJitter -1) mustguard
%
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /Lean -1 >> dygrass } /dygrass-lean-must-be-non-negative
%   (/Lean -1) mustguard
%
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /Direction { 90 } >> dygrass } /dygrass-direction-must-be-a-number
%   (a procedure /Direction) mustguard
%
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /Wander 2 >> dygrass } /dygrass-wander-must-be-0-to-1
%   (/Wander 2) mustguard
%
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /Zigzag 1 >> dygrass } /dygrass-zigzag-must-be-a-boolean
%   (a number /Zigzag) mustguard
%
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 1000000 0 lineto << /Spacing 0.5 >> dygrass }
%   /dygrass-blade-count-exceeds-safety-limit
%   (a tiny spacing on a long line) mustguard
%
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /Zigzag true >> dygrass
%     newpath 5 5 moveto << >> dygrass newpath << >> dygrass }
%   (zigzag grass, a lone point and an empty path) mustpass
%
%   newpath 0 0 moveto 100 0 lineto << /Spacing 10 /Lean 0 /LengthJitter 0 /Wander 0 >> dygrass
%   /dyct 0 def { pop pop /dyct dyct 1 add def } { pop pop } { 6 { pop } repeat } { } pathforall
%   dyct 11 eq
%   (blades every /Spacing along the line) mustbe
%%EndSelfTest
%
% @kind: Procedure
% @summary: Grass as a child draws it: the current path is read as the ground line and replaced with quick blades up from it, /Spacing apart, leaning and of uneven length -- or, with /Zigzag, one continuous up-and-down line without lifting the crayon. Replaces the current path; paints nothing, so `opts dygrass << >> dycrayon`. Deterministic under the caller's own srand, with three draws per blade.
% @example: newpath 20 40 moveto 300 46 lineto << /Spacing 6 /Length 18 >> dygrass << /Width 3.5 >> dycrayon
% @param: /Spacing [points] Distance between blades along the ground line; must be > 0 (default 5)
% @param: /Length [points] Mean blade length; must be > 0 (default 14)
% @param: /LengthJitter [fraction of /Length] 0..1 how far each blade's length varies around /Length (default 0.4)
% @param: /Lean [degrees] Random lean of each blade around /Direction; must be >= 0 (default 14)
% @param: /Direction [degrees] Heading of the blades, counterclockwise from +x in user space (default 90, straight up)
% @param: /Wander [fraction of /Spacing] 0..1 how far each blade's foot slides along the line from its even slot (default 0.4)
% @param: /Zigzag [boolean] Join each blade's tip to the next blade's foot in one continuous line (default false)
/dygrass {
    dup type /dicttype ne { pop dygrass-options-must-be-a-dict } if
    /dyGO exch def
    /dyGsp dyGO /Spacing 5 1e-6 1e6 /dygrass-spacing-must-be-positive dyoptnum def
    /dyGl dyGO /Length 14 1e-6 1e6 /dygrass-length-must-be-positive dyoptnum def
    /dyGj dyGO /LengthJitter 0.4 0 1 /dygrass-lengthjitter-must-be-0-to-1 dyoptnum def
    /dyGlean dyGO /Lean 14 0 1e6 /dygrass-lean-must-be-non-negative dyoptnum def
    /dyGdir dyGO /Direction 90 -1e6 1e6 /dygrass-direction-must-be-a-number dyoptnum def
    /dyGw dyGO /Wander 0.4 0 1 /dygrass-wander-must-be-0-to-1 dyoptnum def
    /dyGz dyGO /Zigzag false /dygrass-zigzag-must-be-a-boolean dyoptbool def
    dyGsp 50000 { dygrass-blade-count-exceeds-safety-limit } dyCcollect
    newpath
    dyCsubs {
        aload pop /dyGb exch def /dyGa exch def
        dyGa 1 dyGb {
            /dyGi exch def
            dyCs dyGi get aload pop
            /dyGend exch def /dyGsp1 exch def pop /dyGang exch def /dyGy exch def /dyGx exch def
            /dyGfw frnd def /dyGfl frnd def /dyGfj frnd def
            % walkpath's closing stop can sit just past the last regular one
            dyGend 2 and 2 eq dyGsp1 dyGsp 0.5 mul lt and dyGi dyGa gt and not {
                /dyGo dyGfw 2 mul 1 sub dyGw mul dyGsp mul 0.5 mul def
                /dyGfx dyGx dyGang cos dyGo mul add def
                /dyGfy dyGy dyGang sin dyGo mul add def
                /dyGh dyGdir dyGfl 2 mul 1 sub dyGlean mul add def
                /dyGlen dyGl 1 dyGfj 2 mul 1 sub dyGj mul add mul def
                dyGz dyGi dyGa gt and { dyGfx dyGfy lineto } { dyGfx dyGfy moveto } ifelse
                dyGfx dyGh cos dyGlen mul add dyGfy dyGh sin dyGlen mul add lineto
            } if
        } for
    } forall
} def
